ρ ˆ± (G, m, N0) = min {|Σ± A| |A ⊆ G, |A|= m}

Chapter E: The critical number
E.1: Unrestricted sumsets:
χ (G, h ) = min {m |A ⊆ G, |A|= m ⇒ hA = G}
χ (G, [0, s ]) = min {m |A ⊆ G, |A|= m ⇒ [0, s ]A = G}
χ (G, N0) = min {m |A ⊆ G, |A|= m ⇒ ⟨ A⟩ = G}
E.2: Unrestricted signed sumsets:
χ ± (G, h ) = min {m |A ⊆ G, |A|= m ⇒ h± A = G}
χ ± (G, [0, s ]) = min {m |A ⊆ G, |A|= m ⇒ [0, s ]± A = G}
χ ± (G, N0) = min {m |A ⊆ G, |A|= m ⇒ ⟨ A⟩ = G}

E.3: Restricted sumsets:
χˆ (G, h ) = min {m |A ⊆ G, |A|= m ⇒ hˆA = G}
χˆ (G, [0, s ]) = min {m |A ⊆ G, |A|= m ⇒ [0, s ] ˆA = G}
χˆ (G, N0) = min {m |A ⊆ G, |A|= m ⇒ ΣA = G}
E.4: Restricted signed sumsets:
χ ˆ± (G, h ) = min {m |A ⊆ G, |A|= m ⇒ hˆ± A = G}
χ ˆ± (G, [0, s ]) = min {m |A ⊆ G, |A|= m ⇒ [0, s ]ˆ± A = G}
χ ˆ± (G, N0) = min {m |A ⊆ G, |A|= m ⇒ Σˆ± A = G}

Chapter F: Zero-sum-free sets
F.1: Unrestricted sumsets:
τ(G, h ) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ̸∈ hA}
τ(G, [1, t ]) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ̸∈ [1, t ]A}
F.2: Unrestricted signed sumsets:
τ± (G, h ) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ̸∈ h± A}
τ± (G, [1, t ]) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ̸∈ [1, t ]± A}
F.3: Restricted sumsets:
τˆ (G, h ) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ̸∈ hˆA}
τˆ (G, [1, t ]) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ̸∈ [1, t ] ˆA}
τˆ (G, N) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ̸∈ [1, m ] ˆA}
F.4: Restricted signed sumsets:
τ ˆ± (G, h ) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ̸∈ hˆ± A}
τ ˆ± (G, [1, t ]) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ̸∈ [1, t ]ˆ± A}
τ ˆ± (G, N) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ̸∈ [1, m ]ˆ± A}

Chapter G: Sum-free sets
G.1: Unrestricted sumsets:
µ (G, {k, l }) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, kA ∩ lA = ∅}
µ (G, [0, s ]) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ≤ l < k ≤ s ⇒ kA ∩ lA = ∅}
G.2: Unrestricted signed sumsets:
µ ± (G, {k, l }) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, k ± A ∩ l± A = ∅}
µ ± (G, [0, s ]) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ≤ l < k ≤ s ⇒ k± A ∩ l± A = ∅}
G.3: Restricted sumsets:
µˆ (G, {k, l }) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, k ˆA ∩ lˆA = ∅}
µˆ (G, [0, s ]) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ≤ l < k ≤ s ⇒ kˆA ∩ lˆA = ∅}
µˆ (G, N0) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ≤ l < k ⇒ kˆA ∩ lˆA = ∅}

G.4: Restricted signed sumsets:
µ ˆ± (G, {k, l }) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, kA ∩ lA = ∅}
µ ˆ± (G, [0, s ]) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ≤ l < k ≤ s ⇒ k ˆ± A ∩ l ˆ± A = ∅}
µ ˆ± (G, N0) = max {|A| |A ⊆ G, 0 ≤ l < k ⇒ k ˆ± A ∩ l ˆ± A = ∅}

