Problem D.49 Classify all situations when
ρˆ (Zn, m, h ) < uˆ (n, m, h );
in particular, how much smaller than uˆ (n, m, h ) can ρˆ (Zn, m, h ) be?

Conjecture D.82 Let p be the smallest prime divisor of n, A be an m-subset of G, and
assume that p > hm − h2 + 1. Then |hˆA|= hm − h2 + 1 if, and only if, (at least) one of
the following holds:
(i) h = 1 (and A arbitrary);
(ii) h = m − 1 (and A arbitrary);
(iii) h = 2, m = 4, and A is of the form A = {a, a + d1, a + d2, a + d1 + d2} (for arbitrary
a, d 1, d 2 ∈ G);
(iv) A is an arithmetic progression (of size m).

Problem D.96 Find a function f (h) (as “small” as possible) for which
ρˆ (G, m, h ) ≤ min{ρ(G, m, h ), hm − h2 + 1 + f (h)}
holds for any G, m, and h.
